# Build context for `docker build -f cluster/deploy/docker/Dockerfile[.operator] .` (from
# the repository root). BuildKit reads this file automatically because it sits
# next to the Dockerfile. Allow-list: the cluster workspace (cluster/) depends
# by path on crates/ (engine, http, rustic-core), whose `*.workspace = true`
# keys are inherited from the root Cargo.toml (itself a package: src/main.rs
# must exist for cargo to load it). Nothing else is needed: no
# bench/, tests/, docs/, or build outputs. (~10 MB context.)
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!src
!crates
!cluster
**/target
**/target-*
**/.DS_Store
**/__pycache__
**/*.mov
cluster/docs
cluster/deploy/helm
cluster/deploy/k8s
cluster/deploy/operator
cluster/scripts
